title Knowbook tags
buildConcepts tags.js

// Editorial classification v5, 2026-09-16. Source: catalog.scroll titles and comments.
// Strategy: combine broad subject splits with independent activity and time axes.
// Prefer questions that separate meaningful groups; retain narrower questions for
// useful branches (plants, electricity, collaboration). These are candidate tree
// features, not a claim that one fixed question order is an optimal decision tree.
// Membership is inferred from the central topic and its typical learning activities,
// not verified kit contents. A missing ID means editorial No under that scope.
// Timing describes learning opportunities, not completion promises. Hazard means
// the real phenomenon warrants care, not that the shipped kit is unsafe; No is not
// a safety guarantee. Revisit assignments when experiment descriptions exist.
// Plant involvement includes plant-derived materials. Multiple people means real
// interpersonal practice is central, even when a solo simulation is possible.
// Rebuild with: scroll list | scroll build
// Search examples: plantTag; chemistryTag; seeds; startups. Tags stay off product cards.
// Keywords are search aliases, not additional vector dimensions.
// Similarity uses Jaccard distance across all tag answers: shared Yes / either Yes.
// Require at least 75% overlap and show at most six additional neighbors.
// Exact titles/IDs precede partial titles, tag matches, then similar knowbooks.

idParser
 extends abstractIdParser
 description Stable searchable tag identifier.

questionParser
 extends abstractStringMeasureParser
 description Yes/no question about the knowbook's central topic or typical activities.

knowbooksParser
 extends abstractStringMeasureParser
 description Space-separated catalog IDs with an editorial Yes answer.

keywordsParser
 extends abstractStringMeasureParser
 description Optional space-separated search aliases for this tag.

